{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An interval tree: a sorted collection of half-open intervals with a value each, which finds the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"intervals overlapping a range, containing a point, or lying within a range in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"k"}]},{"type":"text","text":" + 1) log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") for "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"k","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" results."}],"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/SK","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/Sl","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/SQ","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/Sk","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/ST"],"kind":"relationships"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IntervalTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Bound"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bound"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Comparable"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The intervals are kept in an AVL tree ordered by lower bound, then upper bound, then the order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they were inserted in, and each vertex also records the largest upper bound in its subtree, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a search skips every subtree that ends before the query begins (Cormen, Leiserson, Rivest and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Stein, "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Introduction to Algorithms"}]},{"type":"text","text":", §14.3). The same interval may be stored more than once,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with different values."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var meetings = IntervalTree<Int, String>()","meetings.insert(9 ..< 10, value: \"stand-up\")","meetings.insert(10 ..< 12, value: \"design review\")","meetings.insert(11 ..< 13, value: \"lunch\")","meetings.containing(11).map(\\.value)          \/\/ [\"design review\", \"lunch\"]","meetings.overlapping(9 ..< 11).map(\\.value)   \/\/ [\"stand-up\", \"design review\"]","meetings.contained(in: 9 ..< 12).map(\\.range) \/\/ [9 ..< 10, 10 ..< 12]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Intervals are half-open, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"9 ..< 10"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"10 ..< 12"},{"type":"text","text":" touch without overlapping. As a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collection, the tree’s elements are its entries in that order, read by in-order position."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/rangetrees\/intervaltree"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees"]]},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","title":"IntervalTree","externalID":"s:10RangeTrees12IntervalTreeV","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IntervalTree"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson